  "synthesis_conclusions": [
    "The study revealed main research themes and their relations, as well as connections between spatial cognition and architecture over the past two decades.",
    "Embodied spatial cognition and affordances of architectural design provide a robust framework to guide further investigation in the field.",
    "Future studies should investigate human experience of architecture more holistically, incorporating multisensory spatial information and relevant contextual variables beyond visual sensory information."
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "A gap exists between the constructs, terminologies, and research methods of architecture and neuroscience.",
    "There is a lack of systematic theoretical and empirical frameworks to guide research at the intersection of neuroscience and architecture.",
    "Existing research in the field relies predominantly on visual sensory information, often from 2D images, neglecting embodied and multisensory aspects of human-built environment interaction.",
    "Many studies are based on assumptions about design characteristics and their effects on people, merely reflecting prior observations and 'common sense' knowledge, lacking scientific verification."
  ],
